.\" ai-tools-assets(5) -- the shared skill and subagent sets a sandboxed agent loads.
.\" @AI_TOOLS_VERSION@ is substituted at deploy time (install.sh install_subst
.\" and the RPM %prep), like ai-tools(1).
.TH AI-TOOLS-ASSETS 5 "" "ai-tools @AI_TOOLS_VERSION@" "Agent Tools Restricted"
.SH NAME
ai-tools-assets \- the shared skill and subagent sets a sandboxed agent loads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.BI AI_TOOLS_ASSETS=[ SET / KIND / NAME ", ...]"
.IB /usr/local/share/ai-tools-assets/ SET /
.IB /usr/share/ai-tools-assets/ SET /
.I /usr/share/ai-tools/
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Enable the skill
.B ai\-tools\-reftags
from the set
.BR core ,
once the set's package is installed:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo dnf install ai\-tools\-assets\-core
sudo ai\-tools\-admin assets enable core/skills/ai\-tools\-reftags
.EE
.RE
.PP
An asset set is a directory of skills and subagent definitions published
together, installed by a package under
.IR /usr/share/ai\-tools\-assets/ .
Installing a set does not change what any session loads: an asset reaches
a session only once
.B AI_TOOLS_ASSETS
in
.BR ai-tools-operator.conf (5)
names it, and only while its set verifies.
.PP
An asset is named
.IB SET / KIND / NAME\fR,
the string
.B AI_TOOLS_ASSETS
holds and
.B "ai\-tools\-admin assets"
takes.
.I SET
and
.I NAME
are 1 to 64 characters of
.BR a\-z ,
.B 0\-9
and single hyphens, starting and ending with a letter or digit.
.I KIND
is
.B skills
or
.BR subagents ;
a set keeps its subagents in a directory named
.BR agents/ ,
and the identifier still spells
.BR subagents .
.PP
A linked asset appears as one link under
.I /opt/ai\-tools/skills
or
.IR /opt/ai\-tools/subagents ,
the view every agent reads, and each enabled agent that reads that kind gets
a link to it in its own directory.
An asset is offered to every enabled agent that reads its kind; a note on what
it was written and tested for is the skill's own
.B compatibility
frontmatter field.
.SS The roots
A set is read from the first of three roots that holds it:
.TP
.IB /usr/local/share/ai\-tools\-assets/ SET /
A set you place by hand.
It links only where it verifies against the binding shipped for its name, so
an official release copied here works and an unsigned tree does not.
.TP
.IB /usr/share/ai\-tools\-assets/ SET /
A set a package installed.
.TP
.I /usr/share/ai\-tools/
The set
.B ai\-tools
itself, when it holds a
.IR set.conf .
.PP
The first root that holds an asset wins, asset by asset, so a local copy of
.B core
holding one skill overrides that skill alone.
A copy that is refused does not fall through to the next root: the asset is
reported with the copy's reason.
.SS What a set must be to link
Each set is read in this order, and the first refusal stops it:
every file under it is owned by root and not writable by group or other;
its tree holds regular files and directories alone, within the format's size
bounds; its
.I SHA256SUMS.asc
is a signature by a key the binding for its name pins, over a
.I SHA256SUMS
that lists every file of the set; and its
.I set.conf
and each asset follow the rules of format 1 that base enforces.
A set refused at any step links none of its assets.
.PP
An asset that runs a command when it loads \(em
.B !`command`
in the text, or a fenced block whose language carries
.B !
\(em links only where its
.I metadata/skills/NAME/asset.conf
declares
.B skills.dynamic.v1
in
.BR requires_capabilities ;
the capability is then printed beside the asset.
.PP
An asset requires the asset formats (profiles) it is written in, and every
enabled agent that reads its kind must implement each one, as its manifest
states in
.B asset_profiles
.RB ( ai-tools-providers (5)),
or the asset links for no agent.
.SH REASONS
.B "ai\-tools\-admin assets reconcile"
writes one record per entry of
.BR AI_TOOLS_ASSETS ,
.B linked
or the reason it is not, and
.B "ai\-tools\-admin status"
prints each entry that is not linked with its reason.
A record stream follows
.BR ai-tools-records (5).
.TP
.B id\-malformed
The entry is not
.IB SET / KIND / NAME
under the name grammar, or
.B AI_TOOLS_ASSETS
is not a valid list, which reads as the empty list.
Correct the line.
.TP
.B kind\-unknown
.I KIND
is neither
.B skills
nor
.BR subagents .
A subagent is spelled
.BR subagents .
.TP
.B set\-absent
No root holds the set.
Install its package; the entry links once it is there.
.TP
.B set\-unbound
No binding under
.I /usr/local/lib/ai\-tools/assets\-bindings.d
names the set, so no key may sign it on this host.
.TP
.B path\-untrusted
A root, the set's directory, or a file under it is not owned by root, or is
writable by group or other.
The detail names the path.
Reinstall the set's package, and find out how the path came to be writable.
.TP
.B set\-invalid
The set breaks a rule of format 1 that applies to the whole set; the detail
names the rule and the path.
The set's publisher fixes it in a new release.
.TP
.B set\-tampered
The set's files are not the ones its signature covers.
Reinstall the package; a copy under the local root is replaced from its
release.
.TP
.B set\-unverified
The signature could not be checked: no
.IR SHA256SUMS.asc ,
a key the binding does not name,
.BR gpgv (1)
missing, or a binding or keyring that does not read or is not root's alone.
The detail says which.
.TP
.B requires\-base
The set needs a newer
.BR ai\-tools\-base .
Upgrade it.
.TP
.B capability\-unknown
The set or the asset requires a capability this release does not define.
Upgrade
.BR ai\-tools\-base ,
or leave the asset disabled.
.TP
.B capability\-unsupported
An enabled agent that reads the asset's kind does not implement a profile the
asset requires; the detail names the agent.
The asset links for no agent while that agent is enabled.
.TP
.B receivers\-unknown
The enabled agents could not be read: a provider reader failed, or an input
it reads is not root's alone, so no profile can be checked.
No asset is linked into the view and no agent's directory is changed; one
record names the reader and why, and the command exits 5.
.TP
.B integration\-off
The set or the asset needs an integration that
.B AI_TOOLS_INTEGRATIONS
does not enable.
.TP
.B asset\-absent
The set does not hold that asset.
.TP
.B asset\-invalid
The asset breaks a rule of format 1; the detail names the rule.
The other assets of the set still link.
.TP
.B name\-clash
Two enabled entries from different sets name the same skill or subagent;
neither links.
Disable one.
.TP
.B view\-occupied
A file, a directory or a link of yours stands at the asset's name in the
view; it is left as it is, and the asset is not linked.
.TP
.B agent\-occupied
An agent's own directory holds an entry of yours at an enabled asset's name;
that agent keeps loading yours.
.TP
.B agent\-entry\-untrusted
That entry is not owned by root all the way down, so a session can rewrite
what every later session of that agent loads.
Move it out, or make it root's.
.TP
.B view\-dir\-untrusted
The view directory of a kind, or
.I /opt/ai\-tools
which holds it, is a symlink, is not owned by root, or is writable by group or
other.
No link of that kind is placed or removed, in the view or in an agent's
directory, and the directory is left as it is; the detail names what was read.
Find out what was placed inside it before you restore it.
.TP
.B agent\-dir\-untrusted
An agent's directory for a kind, or its config directory, is a symlink or is
not owned by root; a kind directory writable by group or other, and a config
directory writable by its group without its sticky bit, are refused too.
No link is placed or removed there, and the directory is left as it is.
.TP
.B view\-foreign
An entry in the view is neither a link these commands placed nor a copy the
package seeds there: a skill of your own, a link elsewhere, a name or a shape
the format does not take, or a copy that is not root's all the way down.
It is left as it is and not linked into an agent's directory, though codex,
which reads the whole view, still loads it until you remove it.
A skill of your own goes in the agent's own directory, where it wins over the
view.
.TP
.B enable\-list\-untrusted
.I /etc/ai\-tools/operator.conf
is not owned by root, or is writable by group or other, so no asset is
enabled and every link is removed.
Restore it to
.B root:root
.BR 0644 .
.TP
.B error
A directory the command reads could not be listed, so no link of that kind
was placed or removed there this run; the record names the directory and why,
and the command exits 5.
An enabled asset of that kind carries the same token.
.TP
.B write\-failed
A link could not be placed or removed; the command exits 1.
.TP
.B not\-enabled
.B "assets disable"
named an identifier
.B AI_TOOLS_ASSETS
does not hold.
.PP
A record of a change carries
.B linked
or
.B unlinked
for a link placed or removed, and
.B kept
for a file of yours left in an agent's directory where the view also holds an
entry.
.SH BINDINGS
A binding pins the keys that may sign one set name.
It is one file per set under
.IR /usr/local/lib/ai\-tools/assets\-bindings.d ,
read as
.B KEY=value
data:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
set=core
signers=[openpgp:67F42DC18BF764B42D82F14256D2F802CF9832E4]
keyring=/usr/local/lib/ai\-tools/keys/dag\-node\-package\-signing.gpg
.EE
.RE
.TP
.B set
The set name, equal to the file's name without
.IR .conf .
.TP
.B signers
The primary fingerprints that may sign the set, each written
.BI openpgp: FINGERPRINT
with 40 hexadecimal digits.
.TP
.B keyring
The binary keyring
.BR gpgv (1)
checks the signature against, an absolute path.
.PP
A binding holding any other key is refused, and so is its set.
The package ships the bindings for
.B core
and
.BR ai\-tools ;
each file, the directory and the keyring are
.B root:root
.BR 0644 ,
the directory
.BR 0755 .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ai\-tools/operator.conf
Holds
.BR AI_TOOLS_ASSETS ,
the one setting that enables an asset.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/ai\-tools/assets\-bindings.d
The shipped bindings.
.TP
.I /opt/ai\-tools/skills
.TQ
.I /opt/ai\-tools/subagents
The view: one link per linked asset, beside the copies the package seeds there.
.TP
.I /run/lock/ai\-tools/assets.lock
The lock every
.B "ai\-tools\-admin assets"
command takes, and every installer or package step that seeds the shared
assets, in a directory only root can enter.
A run that waits more than two minutes for it refuses, with the view and the
agents' links as they were.
.TP
.I /var/log/ai\-tools/assets.log
Each record that needs attention, written by
.BR "ai\-tools\-admin assets" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ai\-tools\-admin (8),
.BR ai-tools-operator.conf (5),
.BR ai-tools-providers (5),
.BR ai-tools-records (5),
.BR gpgv (1).
